<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blackfeet Reservation</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Blackfeet Indian Reservation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Blackfeet Reservation is the home of the Blackfeet Nation, the Piikani or Amskapi Pikuni, in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, east of Glacier National Park, with its headquarters at Browning. Its lands are the remnant of the large territory recognised to the Blackfoot by the Lame Bull Treaty of 1855, reduced by later agreements in the 1870s, 1880s and 1890s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blackfeet-reservation.jpg" alt="Blackfeet Reservation" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Murray Foubister · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blackfeet_Indian_sign_(15987533967).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
